# Vercel upload ALLOWLIST (SPEC R2, HOST-04). Ignore everything, then re-admit what the hosted app needs.
#
# Why an allowlist: the Vercel CLI does not read .gitignore and does not ignore .env by default, so
# without this file a push would upload .env, the data lake, the ledger, the logs and the planning
# files. pyproject.toml and uv.lock stay out on purpose: without them Vercel installs only the root
# requirements.txt (D-12).
#
# Why `!data`, then `data/*`, then the one file: a file under an excluded directory cannot be
# re-included, so the folder is re-admitted, its contents re-ignored, and the cache alone re-admitted.
#
# Why the deny rules come LAST: gitignore semantics are last-match-wins, so these re-exclude anything
# nested inside an admitted folder (a stray .env, a cache, a backup or a key) that would otherwise ship.
#
# tests/unit/test_vercel_project_files.py fails if this file is loosened; scripts/check_upload_list.py
# judges the CLI's real upload list before any deploy.
/*
!index.py
!requirements.txt
!.python-version
!vercel.json
!api
!web
!utils
!conf
!data
data/*
!data/web_cache.duckdb
**/.env*
**/__pycache__/
*.tmp.duckdb
*.wal
*.bak
*.pem
*.key
